class QgsCustomCommitErrorHandler : QObject
{
%Docstring(signature="appended")
Abstract base class that may be implemented to report commit errors of a
vector layer.

QGIS reports these errors in its message bar. A handler allows plugins
to report them in their own way.

.. versionadded:: 4.6
%End

%TypeHeaderCode
#include "qgscustomcommiterrorhandler.h"
%End
  public:
    virtual bool handleCommitErrors( QgsVectorLayer *layer, const QStringList &errors ) = 0;
%Docstring
Called when the commit of the changes of ``layer`` failed with the given
``errors``. If ``True`` is returned, then the handler has reported the
errors and they should not be further reported (e.g. by other
QgsCustomCommitErrorHandler, or by QGIS).

Reimplemented methods should return ``False`` for errors they do not
report.
%End
};

